    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **258 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change makes the owner API return a `displayName` field formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'` from the stored names.\n\nTwo edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `displayName` property (readOnly string) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and it appears in API responses.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added an `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(displayName(owner))\")` on `toOwnerDto`, plus a `displayName(Owner)` default helper that returns `lastName + \", \" + firstName` (null-safe).\n\nBecause both the GET (`RespondWithOwner`) and POST/create (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) responder functions map the stored `Owner` entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the field is derived from the persisted names and returned consistently. The acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName`) now passes, and no existing tests regressed.",
